{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/master/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "ansible-doctor",
          "version": "0.9.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/thegeeklab/ansible-doctor",
          "semanticVersion": "0.9.0",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "E101",
              "name": "YAMLSyntaxError",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "YAML syntax error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "YAML file contains syntax errors that prevent parsing. Common causes include incorrect indentation, missing colons, or improperly quoted strings."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Check YAML indentation (Ansible requires 2-space indents). Validate syntax with `yamllint`. Ensure special characters are quoted.",
                "markdown": "## YAML Syntax Error\n\n**Common Causes:**\n- Incorrect indentation (must use 2 spaces, not tabs)\n- Missing colons after keys\n- Unquoted strings with special characters (`:`, `[`, `]`, `{`, `}`)\n\n**Solutions:**\n1. Run `yamllint tasks/main.yml` to identify issues\n2. Check that all keys have colons: `name: value`\n3. Quote strings with special characters: `msg: \"Value: {{ var }}\"`\n\n**Example:**\n```yaml\n# ❌ Wrong (missing colon)\n- name Install nginx\n  apt:\n    name: nginx\n\n# ✅ Correct\n- name: Install nginx\n  apt:\n    name: nginx\n```"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.ansible.com/ansible/latest/reference_appendices/YAMLSyntax.html",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "parsing",
                "tags": ["yaml", "syntax"]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "E201",
              "name": "MissingRequiredAnnotation",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Missing required annotation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Role, collection, or project is missing a required annotation. Annotations provide metadata for documentation generation."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Add required @meta annotation to file header. Example: @meta description: Role configures web server",
                "markdown": "## Missing Required Annotation\n\n**Required Annotations:**\n- `@meta description: <text>` - High-level description of component\n- `@var <name>: <description>` - Description of default variables\n\n**Example:**\n```yaml\n# roles/webserver/meta/main.yml\n# @meta description: Installs and configures nginx web server\n# @meta author: DevOps Team\n\ngalaxy_info:\n  author: devops\n  description: Web server role\n```"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ansible-doctor.example.com/annotations",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "validation",
                "tags": ["annotation", "metadata"]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "W201",
              "name": "MissingRecommendedAnnotation",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Missing recommended annotation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Optional but recommended annotation is missing. Adding this annotation improves documentation quality."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Add @var annotation for better documentation. Example: @var webserver_port: Port for nginx to listen on",
                "markdown": "## Missing Recommended Annotation\n\n**Recommended Annotations:**\n- `@var <name>: <description>` - Document variable purpose and usage\n- `@meta license: <license>` - Specify role license\n- `@meta version: <semver>` - Track role version\n\n**Example:**\n```yaml\n# roles/webserver/defaults/main.yml\n# @var webserver_port: Port for nginx to listen on (default: 80)\nwebserver_port: 80\n\n# @var webserver_ssl_enabled: Enable HTTPS support\nwebserver_ssl_enabled: false\n```"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ansible-doctor.example.com/annotations#recommended",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "validation",
                "tags": ["annotation", "documentation"]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "invocations": [
        {
          "executionSuccessful": false,
          "startTimeUtc": "2025-12-03T10:30:40.000Z",
          "endTimeUtc": "2025-12-03T10:30:45.123Z",
          "commandLine": "ansible-doctor generate . --error-format sarif --error-output results.sarif",
          "workingDirectory": {
